<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Augusto César Sandino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1895">1895</a>–<a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Augusto César Sandino was a Nicaraguan revolutionary who led a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Marines occupying Nicaragua from 1927 to 1933, after rejecting the American-brokered peace that ended the Constitutionalist War. Operating from the northern mountains of Las <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segovia">Segovias</a>, he became a symbol of anti-imperialism across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a>. After the Marines left he made peace, but he was murdered in February 1934 on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anastasio-somoza-garcia">Anastasio Somoza García</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/augusto-cesar-sandino.jpg" alt="Augusto César Sandino" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Augusto_C%C3%A9sar_Sandino.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
